      explanation: "Morgan's withdrawal of further funding in January 1904 was driven by business logic, not physics. The famous (possibly apocryphal) line — 'If anyone can draw on the power, where do we put the meter?' — captures the fundamental problem: a broadcast utility with no billing mechanism could not be monetized by a private investor. Marconi's December 1901 transatlantic demonstration is what made Morgan question the investment in the first place, but the meter problem is what made him refuse to continue.",
